===Etymology 1===
Inflected form of {{m|ro|avea}}. Probably an analogical construction based on the old first-person plural or perhaps influenced by similar forms in other languages.<ref>http://dexonline.ro:8080/articol/Despre_leg%C4%83turile_rom%C3%A2nei_cu_albaneza</ref> Compare {{cog|rup|am|am(u)}}; cf. also Albanian {{m|ro|kam||I have}}.

====Verb====
{{head|ro|verb form}}

# {{inflection of|ro|avea||1|s|pres|indc}}
#: (I) [[have]]
# {{inflection of|ro|avea||1|s|pres|subj}}

===Etymology 2===
From old Romanian {{m|ro||amu}}, presumably from an earlier (proto-) Romanian form {{m|ro||aemu}} (attested in Aromanian), from {{inh|ro|la|habēmus}}. The original first-person singular in proto-Romanian was {{m|ro||aibu}}, from Latin {{m|la|habeō}}, but was changed to {{m|ro|am|am(u)}} by analogy with the first-person plural. The form with -v- ({{m|ro|avem}}) in the present form of the verb's main conjugation (as opposed to its use in this form as an auxiliary verb) may have been remade by analogy with {{m|ro|avut}};<ref>http://www.lingv.ro/RRL%201-2%202009%20Nevaci,%20Todi.pdf</ref> {{m|ro||am}} may also be seen as a reduced, clitic form of {{m|ro|avem}}.<ref>https://books.google.com/books?id=MFWOYUHULgsC&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false</ref> Compare similar contracted forms in {{cog|es|-}} and {{cog|pt|hemos}}, {{cog|ca|hem}}, {{cog|vec|òn}}, {{m|vec|aòn}}. See also {{m|ro|ați}}, which has a parallel development.

